WEBVTT

00:17.727 --> 00:22.437
<b>THE ELUSIVE SAMURAI</b>

01:30.047 --> 01:31.307
<b>NORTHERN FRONT
MOCHIZUKI'S MAIN ARMY</b>

01:31.387 --> 01:32.507
<b>Father…</b>

01:33.467 --> 01:35.347
<b><i>-Ayako…</i>
-Father…</b>

01:37.687 --> 01:40.477
<b><i>To lose her father and the battle…</i></b>

01:41.357 --> 01:43.317
<b><i>the pain in her heart</i>
<i>must be unfathomable…</i></b>

01:50.527 --> 01:52.527
<b>So sad!</b>

01:52.617 --> 01:56.457
<b>The incredibly cool Lord Mochizuki
has perished.</b>

01:57.327 --> 01:58.417
<b>Mr. Mochizuki?</b>

01:59.117 --> 02:00.667
<b>Yo! Chojumaru.</b>

02:02.877 --> 02:06.837
<b>Father! I thought you were dead!</b>

02:09.257 --> 02:12.967
<b>Your father is a phoenix, Ayako.
And thank you for coming!</b>

02:13.057 --> 02:16.347
<b>Oh, my gosh! I'm so glad you're all right!</b>

02:16.427 --> 02:17.427
<b>Ah, it hurts…</b>

02:17.517 --> 02:19.557
<b>Father! Too much! You're breaking my ribs!</b>

02:19.647 --> 02:20.647
<b>SQUEEEZE - CRACK</b>

02:20.727 --> 02:21.977
<b>Don't be so fragile.</b>

02:22.057 --> 02:25.067
<b>Us Mochizukis get stronger
with every cracked rib.</b>

02:25.147 --> 02:27.947
<b>You should try it! Go on then!</b>

02:29.657 --> 02:31.027
<b>-Like father, like daughter.
-Like father, like daughter.</b>

02:31.107 --> 02:34.407
<b>Hey, wait. Mr. Mochizuki.</b>

02:34.487 --> 02:35.577
<b>Hmm?</b>

02:35.657 --> 02:39.157
<b>You, Mr. Tokoiwa,
and your army are unharmed?</b>

02:39.917 --> 02:43.037
<b>Did you all just not fight?
Did you just let the fort fall?</b>

02:43.667 --> 02:45.167
<b>Yeah, that's right.</b>

02:45.247 --> 02:48.087
<b>Holing up and fighting on the sly's
just not my style.</b>

02:48.167 --> 02:51.177
<b>They can have the fort, for all I care.</b>

02:52.507 --> 02:53.757
<b>You've got to be kidding!</b>

02:54.387 --> 02:55.387
<b>NORTH</b>

02:55.467 --> 02:57.927
<b>If this place falls,
things are going to get hectic.</b>

02:58.017 --> 03:01.097
<b>At this rate, Ichikawa's army
will make their way south,</b>

03:01.187 --> 03:04.187
<b>and we'll be severely disadvantaged
on the central and southern fronts!</b>

03:04.267 --> 03:06.437
<b>SOUTH
CENTER</b>

03:06.527 --> 03:07.687
<b>Wait.</b>

03:08.487 --> 03:10.317
<b>We are entirely in his debt.</b>

03:10.397 --> 03:12.317
<b>KITAJO MANOR MAGISTRATE
MUNEIE TOKOIWA</b>

03:13.117 --> 03:15.277
<b>Our fort's defenses are weak,</b>

03:15.367 --> 03:17.407
<b>and it cannot house a large army.</b>

03:17.487 --> 03:19.867
<b>It wouldn't last two days
against an opponent like Ichikawa.</b>

03:22.117 --> 03:25.247
<b>If Lord Mochizuki hadn't breached
their siege and let us escape,</b>

03:25.337 --> 03:27.167
<b>not only would the fort have been
completely annihilated,</b>

03:27.247 --> 03:28.417
<b>but so too would all of our troops.</b>

03:29.717 --> 03:30.917
<b>So you see, kid.</b>

03:31.717 --> 03:34.087
<b>We are a much bigger threat
to Ichikawa uninjured</b>

03:34.177 --> 03:36.177
<b>and hiding out here in the mountains.</b>

03:36.257 --> 03:37.307
<b>NORTH
MIDDLE</b>

03:37.387 --> 03:39.217
<b>We can attack him at any time
from the rear</b>

03:39.307 --> 03:41.437
<b>as he tries to make his way
to the central front.</b>

03:42.187 --> 03:44.097
<b>Specifically, when he goes
to cross the river,</b>

03:44.187 --> 03:45.767
<b>he'll essentially be a sitting duck.</b>

03:45.857 --> 03:47.147
<b>I see.</b>

03:47.227 --> 03:49.607
<b>So a coordinated pincer attack with
Shinomiya's army on the opposite shore</b>

03:49.687 --> 03:51.567
<b>could be just
the devastating blow we need.</b>

03:52.527 --> 03:53.987
<b>What a marvelous plan.</b>

03:54.527 --> 03:58.157
<b>I'm assuming you've already made contact
with Mr. Shinomiya then?</b>

04:01.157 --> 04:03.207
<b>Shinomiya?</b>

04:03.287 --> 04:05.627
<b>So you haven't made contact with him!</b>

04:05.707 --> 04:09.667
<b>But that means Ichikawa's going
to make it across the river, Father!</b>

04:09.757 --> 04:12.877
<b>Which means Mr. Shinomiya is going
to be the one to get pincer attacked!</b>

04:12.967 --> 04:14.377
<b>All right! I'm sorry, okay?</b>

04:14.467 --> 04:17.467
<b>We only just got out from the fort.
I didn't have time to plan that far ahead!</b>

04:17.547 --> 04:19.557
<b>-Father!
-We'd better hurry</b>

04:19.637 --> 04:20.677
<b>and let Mr. Shinomiya know.</b>

04:20.767 --> 04:24.097
<b>Yes. Ichikawa's army
will be on the move tomorrow morning.</b>

04:25.647 --> 04:29.357
<b>Ayako. You stay here
and help defend your father.</b>

04:30.477 --> 04:31.527
<b>But…</b>

04:31.607 --> 04:32.647
<b>Starting tomorrow,</b>

04:32.737 --> 04:35.607
<b>I'm leaving messenger duty for the
northern and central fronts to you too.</b>

04:36.157 --> 04:39.657
<b>Now's your chance
to fight alongside your father.</b>

04:39.737 --> 04:41.537
<b>Be a good daughter, and do him proud.</b>

04:45.037 --> 04:46.247
<b>Certainly!</b>

04:47.537 --> 04:49.877
<b>He may be helplessly lacking in stature,</b>

04:49.957 --> 04:52.457
<b>but that Young Lord of yours
sure has the guts</b>

04:52.547 --> 04:54.007
<b>to be a military commander.</b>

04:54.677 --> 04:55.757
<b>Yes.</b>

04:55.837 --> 04:58.257
<b>I'm finding myself more and more devoted
by the day.</b>

04:58.347 --> 04:59.557
<b>It's becoming quite the hassle.</b>

05:09.057 --> 05:12.067
<b>CENTRAL FRONT
SHINOMIYA'S MAIN ARMY</b>

05:12.817 --> 05:14.697
<b>And so, Mr. Shinomiya,</b>

05:14.777 --> 05:18.197
<b>could you please station some soldiers
at the exit to the northern mountains?</b>

05:18.817 --> 05:19.987
<b>-Do it.
-Yes, my lord.</b>

05:20.077 --> 05:21.617
<b>You need only spare a few.</b>

05:21.697 --> 05:23.157
<b>Thank you, Mr. Messenger.</b>

05:23.747 --> 05:28.327
<b>I'd love to hear more,
but you should rest in Hoshina's camp.</b>

05:31.337 --> 05:33.587
<b>He's grown so much in just one year.</b>

05:34.417 --> 05:36.217
<b>I can't wait to see what the future holds.</b>

05:37.627 --> 05:41.557
<b>CENTRAL FRONT
HOSHINA'S MAIN ARMY</b>

05:47.387 --> 05:49.687
<b>I can't eat any more…</b>

06:04.037 --> 06:05.117
<b>Forward!</b>

06:06.247 --> 06:08.997
<b>MOCHIZUKI
ICHIKAWA</b>

06:09.077 --> 06:11.787
<b>SHINOMIYA - NEZU
PROVINCIAL OFFICIAL</b>

06:11.877 --> 06:14.757
<b>MOCHIZUKI
HOSHINA</b>

06:15.337 --> 06:17.217
<b>Mochizuki hasn't changed at all.</b>

06:17.797 --> 06:19.087
<b>He is careless in his actions,</b>

06:19.177 --> 06:21.637
<b>but somehow, things always seem
to work out for the better for him.</b>

06:22.717 --> 06:25.467
<b>Now, with our newfound knowledge
of what's going on in the north,</b>

06:25.557 --> 06:26.887
<b>we shall hold a war council meeting.</b>

06:27.557 --> 06:30.477
<b>Sure enough, what is most important
for the central front now</b>

06:30.557 --> 06:32.017
<b>is to defeat the provincial official.</b>

06:32.107 --> 06:34.527
<b>I'd like to make it a quick
and decisive battle,</b>

06:35.687 --> 06:37.817
<b>but we are evenly matched
with the provincial official's army,</b>

06:37.897 --> 06:39.357
<b>and we do not have a trump card.</b>

06:40.857 --> 06:43.367
<b>Is there any way out of this deadlock?</b>

06:47.657 --> 06:48.707
<b>Mr. Nezu.</b>

06:50.167 --> 06:53.337
<b>May I offer some advice
from the perspective of a messenger?</b>

06:57.667 --> 07:00.927
<b>Fubuki.
What you were talking about yesterday.</b>

07:05.057 --> 07:08.017
<b>We saw the fort in the south yesterday.</b>

07:08.887 --> 07:11.477
<b>We believe the military forces
sent to the fort were somewhat excessive.</b>

07:12.017 --> 07:13.017
<b>Excessive?</b>

07:13.647 --> 07:15.517
<b>The fort is structurally sound.</b>

07:16.397 --> 07:18.987
<b>If we can predict the direction
of their attack in advance,</b>

07:19.647 --> 07:22.697
<b>we should be able to defend it with
Mr. Unno's army and a few extra soldiers.</b>

07:23.777 --> 07:26.947
<b>We would need a large number of scouts
to pull it off,</b>

07:27.787 --> 07:29.957
<b>but even an army at 80% capacity
would be sufficient.</b>

07:30.037 --> 07:31.457
<b>UNNO'S ARMY + INUKAI'S ARMY
224 SOLDIERS</b>

07:31.537 --> 07:35.127
<b>One, two, three, four, five…</b>

07:35.207 --> 07:36.707
<b>BAD AT MATH</b>

07:36.797 --> 07:38.457
<b>I see.</b>

07:38.547 --> 07:41.257
<b>If we send the 50 remaining cavalrymen
to the central front,</b>

07:41.337 --> 07:43.177
<b>they should be quite the valuable asset.</b>

07:47.177 --> 07:48.267
<b>Fubuki.</b>

07:48.347 --> 07:52.897
<b>Could Mr. Nezu not send in his hawk
to surveil the fort?</b>

07:54.727 --> 07:58.477
<b>Of course!
Then we won't need so many scouts.</b>

07:58.567 --> 08:01.067
<b>If we leave 100 cavalrymen in the south,
they can hold out for ten days.</b>

08:03.107 --> 08:04.357
<b>A decisive battle of brief duration</b>

08:04.447 --> 08:07.327
<b>also won't require as many reservists
at the fort.</b>

08:07.987 --> 08:12.037
<b>So, in exchange
for sending Mr. Nezu south,</b>

08:12.117 --> 08:16.497
<b>we could pull 200 troops from the south
to converge on the central front.</b>

08:17.837 --> 08:19.957
<b>That is always a possibility.</b>

08:24.837 --> 08:25.837
<b><i>Shizuku.</i></b>

08:27.927 --> 08:29.137
<b>What a brilliant idea.</b>

08:29.677 --> 08:30.967
<b>Thanks to Mr. Nezu,</b>

08:31.057 --> 08:33.347
<b>we now know pretty much all of
the locations that need extra vigilance</b>

08:33.437 --> 08:34.517
<b>on the central front.</b>

08:35.227 --> 08:37.977
<b>You can leave any future fighting
to just us now.</b>

08:39.477 --> 08:41.487
<b>Your suggestion makes perfect sense.</b>

08:41.567 --> 08:44.947
<b>I feel a little ashamed to be taking
strategic advice from a child, but…</b>

08:45.737 --> 08:47.117
<b>Shizuku.</b>

08:47.197 --> 08:50.367
<b>It is advice coming from you. I know
that Lord Yorishige trusts you deeply.</b>

08:51.747 --> 08:52.957
<b>Very well.</b>

08:53.037 --> 08:54.037
<b>ICHIKAWA - MOCHIZUKI
SHINOMIYA + HOSHINA</b>

08:54.117 --> 08:56.037
<b>The north will keep their army at bay
with a pincer attack,</b>

08:56.877 --> 09:00.207
<b>I will trade places
with 200 men in the south,</b>

09:00.837 --> 09:03.917
<b>and Hoshina's party will settle things
here in the center.</b>

09:04.417 --> 09:06.087
<b>There are well over 500 men.</b>

09:06.177 --> 09:07.717
<b>Chojumaru.</b>

09:07.797 --> 09:09.757
<b>As messenger,
you must know many secret paths.</b>

09:10.347 --> 09:12.307
<b>Let us make haste.
I need you to guide my path southward.</b>

09:12.387 --> 09:13.597
<b>Yes, sir.</b>

09:15.307 --> 09:19.227
<b><i>Shizuku has a lot of influence</i>
<i>over the chief vassals</i></b>

09:19.307 --> 09:21.437
<b><i>due to her being a representative</i>
<i>of Mr. Yorishige.</i></b>

09:25.317 --> 09:28.737
<b><i>Only she could come up</i>
<i>with such a bold idea</i></b>

09:28.817 --> 09:31.407
<b><i>like shuffling the generals around.</i></b>

09:32.617 --> 09:36.917
<b>TOKIYUKI</b>

09:39.497 --> 09:44.917
<b>THE NEXT DAY
SOUTHERN FRONT - FUKASHI FORT</b>

09:47.627 --> 09:51.097
<b>I sent 200 cavalrymen in secret
to the central front last night.</b>

09:51.757 --> 09:54.137
<b>Mr. Nezu and I have also made
all the necessary arrangements</b>

09:54.217 --> 09:55.307
<b>to help defend the fort.</b>

09:56.187 --> 09:59.227
<b>I have a hawk watching the front,
but I can't keep him for long.</b>

10:00.307 --> 10:03.107
<b>Please tell Hoshina
to have the battle on the central front</b>

10:03.187 --> 10:05.737
<b>-finished within three days.
-Yes, sir!</b>

10:08.237 --> 10:10.777
<b>Everyone, I bid you good luck.</b>

10:16.157 --> 10:18.957
<b>The Young Lord is fascinating, Mr. Nezu.</b>

10:19.707 --> 10:20.787
<b>Yes.</b>

10:20.877 --> 10:24.297
<b>To think he enjoys the work
of darting about all the time.</b>

10:25.257 --> 10:27.717
<b>He's a fine lad, I'll give him that,</b>

10:27.797 --> 10:30.427
<b>but should we really be going ahead
with a child's strategy?</b>

10:33.217 --> 10:34.467
<b>What are you getting at?</b>

10:35.557 --> 10:37.637
<b>Defeating the provincial official's army
may only be a numbers game,</b>

10:37.727 --> 10:39.897
<b>but Sadamune is a battle-hardened master.</b>

10:40.767 --> 10:45.147
<b>Just as we have our plan,
he will surely have his own as well.</b>

10:46.647 --> 10:48.317
<b>I want to go home.</b>

10:48.397 --> 10:51.817
<b>Just how much have we been
running around these past few days?</b>

10:51.907 --> 10:54.407
<b>Don't say that, Genba.
You've gotta stick with us.</b>

10:54.487 --> 10:57.617
<b>There may come a time when
we need your power.</b>

10:57.697 --> 11:00.207
<b><i>He's right though.</i>
<i>We are pushing ourselves.</i></b>

11:00.917 --> 11:04.627
<b><i>The Young Lord</i>
<i>may be going too far this time.</i></b>

11:09.757 --> 11:12.927
<b>Mr. Unno. Didn't you say
there were around 100 enemy troops</b>

11:13.007 --> 11:14.887
<b>stationed to the north of the fort?</b>

11:14.967 --> 11:17.427
<b>Yes. They have not moved
since the outbreak of this war.</b>

11:17.927 --> 11:21.307
<b>They're not there.
There are no signs of the enemy there!</b>

11:27.817 --> 11:31.197
<b>TOKIYUKI
SADAMUNE</b>

11:32.867 --> 11:34.237
<b>It's them.</b>

11:34.317 --> 11:35.737
<b>When did they get here?</b>

11:37.827 --> 11:40.827
<b>So, the little restless messenger,
flitting about hither and thither,</b>

11:40.907 --> 11:42.577
<b>was you all along.</b>

11:43.457 --> 11:44.957
<b>Didn't I tell you</b>

11:45.037 --> 11:47.747
<b>that if I saw you on the battlefield,
I would kill you without hesitation?</b>

11:48.377 --> 11:51.047
<b>If I capture you, torture you,</b>

11:51.127 --> 11:53.927
<b>and make you confess every single detail
relating to Suwa's instructions</b>

11:54.007 --> 11:55.797
<b>and their involvement in the war,</b>

11:55.887 --> 11:59.017
<b>not only will I win this war,</b>

11:59.097 --> 12:04.057
<b>it will also give me just cause
to put an end to that Yorishige!</b>

12:04.147 --> 12:10.027
<b>Go, men! All 100 of you!</b>

12:12.817 --> 12:15.407
<b>Show them no mercy,
even if they are children!</b>

12:15.487 --> 12:19.197
<b>With sword in hand,
all are equal on the battlefield!</b>

12:20.037 --> 12:22.037
<b>Sever a limb or two if you have to.</b>

12:22.617 --> 12:25.537
<b>Just make sure you capture them
in a state where they can still talk.</b>

12:26.377 --> 12:29.337
<b>Brat! Kojiro! Abandon the horses!</b>

12:34.427 --> 12:36.757
<b>They haven't fully closed in on us
from the right.</b>

12:36.847 --> 12:38.637
<b>We'll climb the hill,
and make a run for it.</b>

12:38.717 --> 12:39.847
<b>Right.</b>

12:44.937 --> 12:45.977
<b>Ow! What is this?</b>

12:47.307 --> 12:49.317
<b>-Why, you…
-What is this?</b>

12:50.727 --> 12:53.147
<b><i>Another smokescreen from the fox, huh?</i></b>

12:53.857 --> 12:57.617
<b><i>I've already seen that your smokescreen</i>
<i>has a limited range.</i></b>

12:58.447 --> 13:01.697
<b><i>You'll be stepping out from the smoke</i>
<i>just around…</i></b>

13:02.617 --> 13:03.657
<b><i>There!</i></b>

13:08.037 --> 13:09.667
<b>Got him!</b>

13:09.747 --> 13:11.957
<b>We got him!</b>

13:13.507 --> 13:15.007
<b><i>This is bad…</i></b>

13:15.717 --> 13:17.467
<b><i>They caught us.</i></b>

13:19.927 --> 13:21.217
<b><i>We're finished.</i></b>

13:26.897 --> 13:27.897
<b>Huh?</b>

13:27.977 --> 13:29.937
<b>Who was that?</b>

13:30.017 --> 13:32.027
<b>Who was that, you ask?</b>

13:32.107 --> 13:33.937
<b>Well, I'll just have
to give you the answer.</b>

13:34.027 --> 13:37.357
<b>Heaven's net has wide meshes,
but nothing escapes it.</b>

13:37.447 --> 13:39.527
<b>For I am the guardian deity
of all of Shinano,</b>

13:39.617 --> 13:40.907
<b>and nothing slips past my watch.</b>

13:40.987 --> 13:42.907
<b>I am the Shinano Mask!</b>

13:49.417 --> 13:50.837
<b>At your service!</b>

13:53.757 --> 13:55.167
<b><i>-Yorishige.</i>
<i>-Yorishige.</i></b>

13:55.257 --> 13:56.377
<b><i>Yorishige.</i></b>

13:57.127 --> 13:58.467
<b>Allow me to explain!</b>

13:58.547 --> 14:01.097
<b>The Shinano Mask is
the avatar of Shinano itself</b>

14:01.177 --> 14:03.017
<b>who appears whenever danger is afoot!</b>

14:03.097 --> 14:04.887
<b>At times tempestuous,
at times compassionate!</b>

14:04.977 --> 14:06.847
<b>A higher supernatural being
who envelops all of Shinano</b>

14:06.937 --> 14:07.937
<b>in his unconditional love!</b>

14:08.017 --> 14:10.897
<b>He is a legendary hero,
a miracle, admired by all…</b>

14:10.977 --> 14:13.977
<b><i>And standing beside him is</i>
<i>the king of commentary, Mr. Moritaka!</i></b>

14:16.147 --> 14:19.107
<b>No matter which way you look at it,
that's just Yorishige Suwa!</b>

14:19.197 --> 14:21.827
<b>The man's got "fishy business"
down to an art!</b>

14:21.907 --> 14:26.157
<b>I am not! I am the Suwa Mask!</b>

14:26.247 --> 14:30.497
<b>Now you've just called yourself Suwa!
Get your facts straight!</b>

14:30.577 --> 14:32.247
<b>Since you remain unconvinced,</b>

14:32.337 --> 14:34.337
<b>we'll just have to let the facts
speak for themselves.</b>

14:34.417 --> 14:35.707
<b>In these turbulent times,</b>

14:35.797 --> 14:38.257
<b>if you want proof
beyond all reasonable doubt,</b>

14:38.337 --> 14:40.337
<b>you have to catch the culprit in the act.</b>

14:40.427 --> 14:43.217
<b>Will you try, Sadamune?</b>

14:50.307 --> 14:51.647
<b>Fall back!</b>

14:51.727 --> 14:52.937
<b>Lord Sadamune!</b>

14:53.017 --> 14:56.067
<b>We are evenly matched,
and we have the low ground.</b>

14:56.147 --> 14:57.487
<b>Our position is not favorable.</b>

14:57.567 --> 14:59.907
<b>Retreat! Retreat!</b>

15:02.407 --> 15:05.117
<b>They gave up. Just like that.</b>

15:06.077 --> 15:08.157
<b>I knew it. They're retreating east.</b>

15:08.867 --> 15:10.577
<b>Just as I expected, Sadamune.</b>

15:10.667 --> 15:14.417
<b>Sending 100 cavalrymen here
was killing two birds with one stone.</b>

15:16.457 --> 15:19.967
<b>The primary objective
for Sadamune's 100 cavalrymen</b>

15:20.047 --> 15:21.677
<b>was to provide backup
to the central front.</b>

15:22.257 --> 15:24.807
<b>He saw that the southern front
was at a standstill,</b>

15:24.887 --> 15:26.387
<b>and since he had
no immediate use for them,</b>

15:26.467 --> 15:28.227
<b>he sent 100 of his cavalrymen
to the center.</b>

15:28.307 --> 15:30.557
<b>He used the same strategy as us.</b>

15:31.517 --> 15:35.767
<b>And his second objective.
Well, that would be you.</b>

15:37.107 --> 15:39.277
<b>You're the shrine attendant
of Suwa Grand Shrine,</b>

15:39.357 --> 15:41.567
<b>running about the battlefield
on a secret mission.</b>

15:41.657 --> 15:44.197
<b>If he can capture you
and make you divulge everything,</b>

15:44.277 --> 15:46.657
<b>that will give him the perfect excuse
to come after me.</b>

15:48.117 --> 15:51.747
<b>He dispatched those 100 cavalrymen
not just to support the central front,</b>

15:51.827 --> 15:54.587
<b>but also as a net to capture you.</b>

15:55.417 --> 15:59.507
<b>Such a future suddenly came to me,
and I came running as fast as I could,</b>

15:59.587 --> 16:01.757
<b>but things are going to become
far too dangerous going forward.</b>

16:02.427 --> 16:04.137
<b>You've done enough, Lord Tokiyuki.</b>

16:05.007 --> 16:07.757
<b>Let the others handle messenger duty
for now. We're going home.</b>

16:08.387 --> 16:09.807
<b>Going home?</b>

16:09.887 --> 16:12.017
<b>The farther I stray from Suwa,</b>

16:12.097 --> 16:15.057
<b>and the more people
drawn into this battle,</b>

16:15.147 --> 16:17.317
<b>the less accurate my prophecies become.</b>

16:19.147 --> 16:22.567
<b>Now that Sadamune has realized
your strategic worth,</b>

16:23.237 --> 16:25.447
<b>continuing messenger duty
is too dangerous.</b>

16:26.867 --> 16:27.867
<b>No.</b>

16:28.407 --> 16:30.907
<b>I think you should go home too.</b>

16:30.997 --> 16:33.667
<b>You've worked yourself to the bone,
Young Lord.</b>

16:33.747 --> 16:35.957
<b>What he said. You're exhausted,</b>

16:36.037 --> 16:38.297
<b>and that's why
you didn't spot their ambush.</b>

16:38.377 --> 16:42.217
<b>No. I don't want to go home. Not now.</b>

16:45.007 --> 16:46.347
<b>Lord Tokiyuki.</b>

16:46.427 --> 16:50.387
<b>Do you have any idea of the men
who make up the small reinforcements</b>

16:50.467 --> 16:51.807
<b>of the Three Great Generals?</b>

16:52.637 --> 16:55.397
<b>Every one of them believes
the day will come</b>

16:55.477 --> 16:58.567
<b>when Suwa Myojin will rise to champion
the desperately suffering people</b>

16:58.647 --> 17:00.027
<b>of Shinano.</b>

17:00.107 --> 17:03.277
<b>Each and every one of them is willing
to put their life on the line</b>

17:03.357 --> 17:04.447
<b>for this war.</b>

17:05.107 --> 17:08.237
<b>But there is no need
for you to do the same.</b>

17:08.867 --> 17:12.447
<b>Your health is vital
to the shogunate revival.</b>

17:12.537 --> 17:15.787
<b>There is no need for you to be taking
such risks right now. Leave it for--</b>

17:15.867 --> 17:17.417
<b>Don't you get it?</b>

17:19.087 --> 17:21.707
<b>I want to be useful for you!</b>

17:22.877 --> 17:25.627
<b>You bear the weight of destiny
on your shoulders,</b>

17:25.717 --> 17:28.887
<b>but all I've been doing
is taking and taking</b>

17:28.967 --> 17:30.387
<b>without ever giving anything back.</b>

17:32.267 --> 17:35.637
<b>When I look out and see all our allies
united in their faith in you,</b>

17:36.517 --> 17:39.727
<b>I feel like I'm finally
giving back to you,</b>

17:40.437 --> 17:41.777
<b>and it makes me happy.</b>

17:44.067 --> 17:47.107
<b>And even then, do we still have to return?</b>

17:52.237 --> 17:53.747
<b>It should be me saying that.</b>

17:54.497 --> 17:55.537
<b>Mr. Yorishige?</b>

17:56.207 --> 17:57.497
<b>All right!</b>

17:57.577 --> 18:00.747
<b>If you feel that deeply about it,
you can continue on with your duties.</b>

18:00.837 --> 18:03.337
<b>But absolutely no fighting. I forbid it!</b>

18:03.417 --> 18:05.127
<b>Focus on getting the message out,</b>

18:05.217 --> 18:07.757
<b>and only watch over the battle
from the rear.</b>

18:07.837 --> 18:09.217
<b>I will!</b>

18:09.297 --> 18:10.507
<b>Good grief.</b>

18:11.307 --> 18:14.057
<b>Please take 100
of Suwa Grand Shrine's finest cavalrymen</b>

18:14.137 --> 18:15.727
<b>and head straight for the central front.</b>

18:16.597 --> 18:18.897
<b>With this, the battle
is now completely even.</b>

18:18.977 --> 18:22.857
<b>If you get the slightest sense of danger,
remember that you can always flee.</b>

18:26.487 --> 18:30.447
<b>Thank you, Mr. Yorishige. I'll be back.</b>

18:35.247 --> 18:37.407
<b>And there he goes.</b>

18:50.087 --> 18:52.347
<b><i>To bear witness to how much you grow</i>
<i>day by day…</i></b>

18:53.307 --> 18:55.017
<b><i>To receive such high praise…</i></b>

18:56.477 --> 19:00.397
<b><i>It is I who have been taking and taking</i>
<i>without giving anything back.</i></b>

19:16.577 --> 19:19.747
<b>-Attack!
-Attack!</b>

19:23.747 --> 19:27.257
<b>CENTRAL FRONT
THE DECISIVE BATTLE</b>

19:36.767 --> 19:38.597
<b>What of Ichikawa in the north?</b>

19:38.677 --> 19:40.637
<b>We can pin him in place
for the entire day.</b>

19:41.437 --> 19:44.107
<b>-Look out for the big, bad man!
-Since the Mochizuki army is doing a dirty</b>

19:44.187 --> 19:45.937
<b>cleverly striking Ichikawa from the rear.</b>

19:46.017 --> 19:48.397
<b>-Who is this?
-I see. That is reassuring.</b>

19:48.487 --> 19:52.317
<b>And now, I must be off.
I'm off to join my father in battle.</b>

19:52.867 --> 19:56.987
<b>Excellent. Now we can focus
all our efforts on the central front.</b>

19:57.997 --> 20:01.537
<b>Mr. Messenger reports
that Hoshina is also dominating.</b>

20:01.617 --> 20:04.077
<b>Let's settle this once and for all today.</b>

20:06.337 --> 20:08.957
<b>Nice. They're pushing back nicely.</b>

20:09.047 --> 20:11.047
<b>Yeah. I had a quick look around,</b>

20:11.127 --> 20:13.427
<b>and both Hoshina's army
and Shinomiya's army</b>

20:13.507 --> 20:14.757
<b>are in great fighting spirits.</b>

20:15.547 --> 20:17.507
<b>With a battle this chaotic,</b>

20:17.597 --> 20:20.137
<b>not even Sadamune's 100 cavalrymen
can tip the scale.</b>

20:20.887 --> 20:22.597
<b>We can win this war.</b>

20:47.337 --> 20:49.247
<b>What is that?</b>

20:54.257 --> 20:55.257
<b>What?</b>

20:56.387 --> 20:58.307
<b>What on earth is that?</b>

20:58.387 --> 20:59.927
<b>A mikoshi?</b>

21:05.397 --> 21:11.857
<b>I'll flatten you all into the ground,
you lawless scum!</b>

21:11.937 --> 21:14.907
<b>Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!</b>

21:14.987 --> 21:18.157
<b>Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!</b>

21:18.237 --> 21:20.987
<b>Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!</b>

21:21.787 --> 21:24.497
<b>Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!</b>

21:26.207 --> 21:28.377
<b>Heave-ho!</b>

21:28.457 --> 21:30.127
<b>Heave-ho!</b>

21:35.257 --> 21:38.217
<b>Lord Hoshina! We must retreat
and re-establish ourselves--</b>

21:41.717 --> 21:43.927
<b>You bastards!</b>

21:45.557 --> 21:47.477
<b>I've gathered the biggest,
burliest men around,</b>

21:47.557 --> 21:50.897
<b>paying them to carry my mikoshi
and serve as my bodyguards.</b>

21:50.977 --> 21:54.067
<b>And I shall shoot them all
from right here,</b>

21:54.147 --> 21:56.907
<b>in the safety of my own little box.</b>

21:56.987 --> 22:02.237
<b>This is my very own battle mikoshi plan!</b>

22:02.327 --> 22:04.957
<b>Hyaaah!</b>

23:38.127 --> 23:38.967
<b><i>Let's go!</i></b>

23:39.047 --> 23:39.927
<b>EPISODE 17 (YEAR 1335)
THE UNYIELDING</b>
